    "parsing_res_list": [
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Taper per inch</td><td>Large opening minus (in inches)</td><td>Small opening (in inches)</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\">divided by</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\">Length of the member to which the gib will be attached (in inches)</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                84,
                273,
                473,
                454
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 0
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>L -</td><td>Length of sliding member</td><td>10&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>$ \\theta $ -</td><td>Angle of dovetail</td><td>45°</td></tr><tr><td>t -</td><td>Thickness of opening (large end)</td><td>0.500&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>t&#x27; -</td><td>Thickness of opening (small end)</td><td>0.400&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>W -</td><td>Width of gib opening or slot</td><td>2&quot;</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\">Calculation for taper</td></tr><tr><td>$ \\frac{t - t&#x27;}{L} $ equals</td><td colspan=\"2\">$ \\frac{.500&quot; - .400&quot;}{10} $</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                88,
                1095,
                487,
                1347
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>or</td><td>taper per inch = .010 $ ^{11} $</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                505,
                75,
                823,
                100
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ \\begin{array}{l}Small end\\quad=.400^{\\prime\\prime}+.020^{\\prime\\prime}=.420^{\\prime\\prime}\\\\Large end\\quad=.530^{\\prime\\prime}+.0\\not\\ge0^{\\prime\\prime}=.550^{\\prime\\prime}\\\\Length of gib piece\\quad=.13^{\\prime\\prime}\\\\Angle of gib piece\\quad=.45^{\\circ}\\\\Width of gib piece\\quad=\\quad2^{\\prime\\prime}\\\\\\end{array} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                502,
                470,
                900,
                587
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "At small end will be .400\"\nAt large end will be .400\" + .130\" = .530\"",
            "block_bbox": [
                504,
                284,
                901,
                332
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "fastened to the stationary member the latter would be measured instead.",
            "block_bbox": [
                82,
                77,
                448,
                121
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Having at hand the necessary data as to thickness and length, the taper per inch can now be computed by the following formula:",
            "block_bbox": [
                82,
                122,
                486,
                212
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "FORMULA: To find the TAPER per inch.",
            "block_bbox": [
                84,
                230,
                478,
                255
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$  T a p e r p e r i n c h=\\frac{t-t^{\\prime}}{L} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
                170,
                474,
                401,
                518
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Sec. 17.18",
            "block_bbox": [
                86,
                541,
                191,
                564
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Supplementary Calculations for TAPERED GIB",
            "block_bbox": [
                86,
                563,
                388,
                610
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In addition to measuring the gib opening and calculating therefrom the taper per inh, an allowance must be made for fitting the gib. Essentially, this involves a modification of two dimensions of the gib, namely the length (L) and the thickness (t). The calculations must be performed and the complete specifications made known before the machine shop can proceed with the construction of the gib piece.",
            "block_bbox": [
                86,
                630,
                480,
                877
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In order to make clear how these two factors will modify the dimensions taken from the dovetail, an example is supplied as follows:",
            "block_bbox": [
                87,
                876,
                485,
                968
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "EXAMPLE",
            "block_bbox": [
                237,
                987,
                345,
                1010
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 13
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Information - obtained from dovetail openings (assumed case) shown in Fig. 17.14.\nIn this example we decide to have, as a safety factor, an excess length in the machined gib piece of, say, 3\". Now we have",
            "block_bbox": [
                88,
                1021,
                462,
                1089
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 14
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                504,
                119,
                907,
                189
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 14
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Total length of gib piece  $ 10'' + 3'' = 13'' $\nTotal taper in  $ 13'' $  $ 13'' x .010' = .130'' $",
            "block_bbox": [
                505,
                194,
                904,
                242
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": 14,
            "group_id": 16
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Therefore: Thickness of gib piece --",
            "block_bbox": [
                505,
                252,
                866,
                275
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 15,
            "group_id": 17
        },
        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>We will now allow ourselves an additional thickness of .020&quot; for purposes of fitting. Consequently, we must again modify the dimensions of the gib piece as follows:</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                502,
                340,
                901,
                453
            ],
            "block_id": 18,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 18
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This represents the final calculation for the dimensions of the finish machined gib piece. Such measurements are never a matter for guess work but should be closely figured. If the piece is made too thick, extra scraping is necessitated. On the other hand, if the surplus provided is inadequate for good fitting, it results in either an incorrect taper or a poor bearing quality.",
            "block_bbox": [
                503,
                606,
                918,
                830
            ],
            "block_id": 19,
            "block_order": 16,
            "group_id": 19
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Should the length be measured closely, leaving no spare, even a slight scraping error cannot be compensated. Consequently, the operator must either discard the piece and start anew, or be content with a poorly fitting gib.",
            "block_bbox": [
                504,
                830,
                904,
                968
            ],
            "block_id": 20,
            "block_order": 17,
            "group_id": 20
        },
        {
            "block_label": "image",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                522,
                1005,
                900,
                1252
            ],
            "block_id": 21,
            "block_order": null,
            "group_id": 21
        },
        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "Fig. 17.14(b) Rear View of Members.\n(t') thickness",
            "block_bbox": [
                564,
